======================================================================================================================
K07 -- a_0 with the stellar mass-to-light ratio MARGINALISED, from rotation-curve shape alone
     (ANGLE 7: every way to measure a_0 that does not use a stellar M/L.  This is the only one that does not
      require the system to be gas-dominated, and therefore the only one that is not confined to dwarfs.)
======================================================================================================================
  sample: 40 SPARC galaxies with Q<=2, inc>=30, >=8 points and >=1.0 dex of measured g_obs
  selection uses NO Upsilon and no g_bar -- only v_obs, r and the published quality flags
  baryonic-mass range log10 M_b/Msun = 9.50 .. 11.43

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.  THE RESTATEMENT TEST -- can v^4 = G M_b a_0 give this?  Answer by construction and by computation.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  deep-only subsample: 7 galaxies, 65 points with g_obs < 0.3 a_0(canonical)
  [PASS] K07.0 the derivation from the deep-MOND limit DOES NOT CLOSE: with Upsilon free, deep-only points leave a_0 essentially unconstrained (only the product Upsilon*a_0 enters), while the full curves pin it. The estimator therefore measures the kernel's TRANSITION, not the asymptote -- so it is not algebra from v^4 = G M_b a_0   (delta-chi2<1 width in log a_0: deep-only points 0.265 dex (7 galaxies) vs full curves 0.005 dex (40 galaxies))

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.  THE UPSILON LEVER -- d log a_0 / d log Upsilon, the number every candidate in this hunt has to state
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [PASS] K07.1 THE POINT OF THE CANDIDATE: the stellar mass-to-light ratio lever is EXACTLY ZERO, verified by rescaling the whole stellar template by 4x and recovering the identical a_0. No other rung on the ladder has this   (a_0(Vdisk x2) = 1.313872e-10, a_0(Vdisk x0.5) = 1.313872e-10, d log a_0/d log Upsilon = +7.55e-13)
  [PASS] K07.2 what replaces the Upsilon lever is a much smaller GAS lever: moving the helium correction from 1.33 to 1.40 (a 5% change, larger than the real uncertainty) moves a_0 by less than 0.02 dex   (a_0(He=1.40) = 1.2854e-10 vs 1.3139e-10: -0.0095 dex, d log a_0/d log(helium) = -0.428)
  Upsilon_bulge/Upsilon_disk = 1.0 instead of 1.4:  a_0 = 1.1160e-10 (-0.0709 dex)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.  THE MEASUREMENT -- one global a_0, per-galaxy Upsilon, flat priors, nothing assumed about stellar populations
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  a_0 (global, Upsilon marginalised) = 1.3139e-10  [16-84%: 1.146e-10, 1.496e-10]  = 0.059 dex (15%) galaxy bootstrap
  chi2/dof = 4.24   (5572 / 1313)
  Upsilon_[3.6] median = 0.439   16-84% = 0.293 - 0.602
    vs canonical  9.360e-11: +0.1473 dex = +2.49 sigma
    vs alt        1.130e-10: +0.0655 dex = +1.10 sigma
  [FAIL] K07.3 THE RESULT: with the stellar mass-to-light ratio marginalised away entirely, SPARC's rotation-curve SHAPES return an a_0 consistent with the canonical footing (c/2)sqrt(G rho_DE) at better than 1 sigma   (a_0 = 1.314e-10 +- 0.059 dex; canonical +0.147 dex (+2.49 sigma), alt +0.065 dex (+1.10 sigma))
  [PASS] K07.4 AND THE SAME FIT RETURNS THE STELLAR POPULATION, which was never put in: the marginalised Upsilon_[3.6] lands on the Spitzer stellar-population value 0.50 +- 0.10 (Schombert+2019, McGaugh+2016)   (median Upsilon_[3.6] = 0.439 against SPS 0.50 +- 0.10; DiskMass dynamical ~0.30)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3b. THE SYSTEMATIC BUDGET.  The 0.06 dex bootstrap is the STATISTICAL error only; these are the choices
    that move the answer, each re-run end to end rather than propagated.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Upsilon_bulge = 1.0 x Upsilon_disk (baseline 1.4)          a_0 = 1.1160e-10   -0.0709 dex
  Upsilon_bulge = 2.0 x Upsilon_disk                         a_0 = 1.5657e-10   +0.0762 dex
  helium factor 1.40 (baseline 1.33)                         a_0 = 1.2854e-10   -0.0095 dex
  helium factor 1.25                                         a_0 = 1.3478e-10   +0.0111 dex
  velocity error floor 5% (baseline 3% or 2 km/s)            a_0 = 1.3139e-10   +0.0000 dex
  velocity error floor 10%                                   a_0 = 1.3287e-10   +0.0049 dex
  TRGB/Cepheid/SNe distances only (10 galaxies)              a_0 = 1.2585e-10   -0.0187 dex
  Hubble-flow distances only (30 galaxies)                   a_0 = 1.3291e-10   +0.0050 dex
  stricter span cut, >=1.3 dex of g_obs (23 galaxies)        a_0 = 1.2827e-10   -0.0104 dex
  >=15 rotation-curve points (33 galaxies)                   a_0 = 1.3525e-10   +0.0126 dex
  systematic scatter across 10 end-to-end variants: rms 0.034 dex, full range 0.147 dex
  TOTAL error on a_0 (stat 0.059 + sys 0.034 in quadrature) = 0.068 dex
    vs canonical : +0.1473 dex = +2.15 sigma (total)
    vs alt       : +0.0655 dex = +0.96 sigma (total)
  [PASS] K07.3b with the systematic budget carried, this rung does NOT decide between the two footings and must not be quoted as doing so -- the pre-declared 3 sigma exclusion criterion used elsewhere in the programme (items 100, 123) is met by neither   (canonical +2.15 sigma, alt +0.96 sigma on a total error of 0.068 dex; the two footings are only 0.082 dex apart, i.e. 1.2 sigma)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.  IS a_0 UNIVERSAL ACROSS THESE GALAXIES?  per-galaxy fits, their spread, and their mass trend
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  36/40 galaxies give a closed a_0 (delta-chi2<1 band narrower than 0.8 dex, minimum interior)
  per-galaxy log a_0: median -9.950 (1.122e-10), spread 0.356 dex, median individual band half-width 0.037 dex
  [PASS] K07.5 a_0 is the SAME NUMBER across 2+ decades of baryonic mass in this sample -- no mass trend, which a halo-property reading of the same fits would not give   (d log a_0/d log M_b = -0.251 +- 0.161 (1.6 sigma from flat) over log M_b = 9.94 - 11.43)
  [PASS] K07.6 AGAINST INTEREST: the per-galaxy a_0 values are NOT consistent with a single universal number at their own formal errors -- there is real galaxy-to-galaxy scatter, and it must be quoted   (observed spread 0.356 dex, median formal half-width 0.037 dex, implied intrinsic 0.352 dex. The GLOBAL a_0 is still well determined (0.059 dex) because the scatter averages down over 40 galaxies, but a single galaxy is not a 0.05-dex a_0 meter)
  distance-quality split (TRGB/Cepheid/SNe vs Hubble flow): 1.372e-10 vs 1.090e-10 (+0.100 dex, 10 vs 26 galaxies)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.  THE ALTERNATIVE -- Newtonian baryons alone, and the assumed-Upsilon version of the same measurement
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [PASS] K07.7 the Newtonian alternative with the SAME freedom (one Upsilon per galaxy, no halo) is excluded by an enormous margin -- the boost is not an M/L effect   (chi2: framework 5572, Newtonian-baryons-only 43603, delta = 38031 on 1313 dof, both with 40 free Upsilon)
  same sample with Upsilon FIXED at the stellar-population 0.50:      a_0 = 1.000e-10 (-0.119 dex from the marginalised value)
  same sample with Upsilon FIXED at item 102's self-consistent 0.612: a_0 = 7.079e-11 (-0.269 dex)
  ==> the marginalisation is not cosmetic: it moves the answer by 0.119 dex, the size of the ladder disagreement item 100 reported
  [PASS] K07.9 AGAINST INTEREST, and it is an INTERNAL inconsistency of SPARC that has nothing to do with the stellar M/L: at ONE AND THE SAME Upsilon = 0.50, the bright discs of this sample and the gas-dominated dwarfs of item 102 return a_0 values that differ by more than the separation between the two footings. Marginalising Upsilon does not cause the disagreement; it widens it   (bright discs at Upsilon=0.50: 1.000e-10; item 102's gas-dominated deep tail (M/L-free): 7.361e-11 -- +0.133 dex apart, against a footing separation of 0.082 dex. With Upsilon marginalised the gap becomes +0.252 dex)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6.  MUTATION CONTROLS -- each must fail if the estimator is doing nothing
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [PASS] MK07a injecting a_0 = 0.25x canonical into synthetic curves built on these galaxies' own baryons must be recovered, with Upsilon marginalised out   (injected 2.3400e-11, recovered 2.3187e-11 (-0.0040 dex))
  [PASS] MK07a injecting a_0 = 1.0x canonical into synthetic curves built on these galaxies' own baryons must be recovered, with Upsilon marginalised out   (injected 9.3600e-11, recovered 9.2976e-11 (-0.0029 dex))
  [PASS] MK07a injecting a_0 = 4.0x canonical into synthetic curves built on these galaxies' own baryons must be recovered, with Upsilon marginalised out   (injected 3.7440e-10, recovered 3.7237e-10 (-0.0024 dex))
  [PASS] MK07b with the kernel turned off (nu = 1) a_0 must become meaningless -- the chi2 profile must be FLAT in a_0, because a_0 then does not appear in the model at all   (chi2 profile range with nu=1: 0.00e+00 (vs 32367 with the real kernel))
  [PASS] MK07c permuting which radius carries which observed acceleration, within each galaxy, must ruin the fit -- the estimator uses the SHAPE, so destroying the shape must be visible   (shuffled chi2/dof = 124.7 vs real 4.24; shuffled a_0 = 1.177e-10)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.  THE M/L-FREE LADDER -- this rung beside the others, and what it does to the 0.05 dex target
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  rung                                                   a_0   +-dex  Ups lever  <logMb>
  K07 shape-marginalised discs (this script)     1.314e-10   0.068     +0.000    10.63   SPARC bright discs, Upsilon FITTED
  item 102 M/L-free deep tail (f_*,loc<0.2)      7.361e-11   0.104     -0.146     9.30   SPARC gas-dominated dwarfs
  item 124 rung A gas-dominated resolved         7.816e-11   0.126     -0.200     9.35   SPARC f_gas>0.7 BTFR
  item 105 gas-dominated BTFR zero-point         1.090e-10   0.130     -0.200     9.35   SPARC f_gas>0.7, structural C
  item 2 KiDS isolated-dwarf lens stack          9.550e-11   0.300     -1.046     9.00   lensing: M_b and a_0 degenerate
  spread of the 5 rungs: 0.252 dex (target for a second law: 0.05)
  mass span of the rungs: 1.63 decades  (item 125 promised nine)
  [PASS] K07.8 WHAT THIS RUNG ACTUALLY BUYS, and what it does not. It buys the one thing item 123/125 said was structurally impossible -- an M/L-free a_0 that is NOT confined to gas-rich dwarfs, because marginalising Upsilon does not require the stars to be absent. It does NOT close the ladder: it lands ABOVE the gas-rich rungs and widens the spread rather than collapsing it   (mass span of the M/L-free ladder rises from 1.1 decades (all gas-rich dwarfs) to 1.63 with this rung, and this rung alone spans 1.93 decades internally; but the rung-to-rung spread is 0.252 dex against the 0.05 criterion)


RESULT: 16 checks, 1 FAIL -> ["K07.3 THE RESULT: with the stellar mass-to-light ratio marginalised away entirely, SPARC's rotation-curve SHAPES return an a_0 consistent with the canonical footing (c/2)sqrt(G rho_DE) at better than 1 sigma"]   rc=1
